  "details": "Opening URLs in VR mode shared by other users (friends) is unnecessarily inaccessible.\n\nThe current workarounds are (ab)using social links in profile for clickable links, asking a person to repeat that URL in the chatbox several times until it's manually typed by the receiver, taking a photo of the chatbox using a camera with the UI shown, or driving users to an external social platform off from VRChat (\"can you add me on Discord?\").\n\nThis is a proposal to share URLs on droppable pedestals, or send to users an URL link in the instance as a delivered notification.\n\nURLs on pedestals would be the same as any other pedestals: 90 seconds or until I leave the instance, shared publicly, with friends or with members of a group. The visibility uses Allow Pedestal Sharing (enabled by default?) and View Pedestals From settings (defaults to Friends).\n\nSend to Users would follow the recipient's settings for receiving notifications about shared URLs. The visibility uses Allow Direct Sharing (enabled by default?) and Accept Sharing From settings (defaults to Friends).\n\nThe pop-up prompt asking to open an external link in a web browser should be shown either way, at least for untrusted URLs.\n\nThis has security considerations up for debate regarding untrusted URLs, public instances, submission of moderation requests (reporting shared URLs), and safety of the Trust & Safety team reviewing those moderation reports.\n\nRelated: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/1222-share-url-links-with-chatbox-open-webpage",
